WEBVTT

00:10:56.191 --> 00:11:00.394
is by watching the attorneys around me
for the whole time I was practicing

00:11:00.418 --> 00:11:03.273
and noticing that there were some
who were effective

00:11:03.297 --> 00:11:08.260
in the kind of stereotypical, you know,
taking over the room

00:11:08.284 --> 00:11:10.021
in a really charismatic kind of way,

00:11:10.045 --> 00:11:11.798
and others who got there

00:11:11.822 --> 00:11:16.315
through a really quiet and cerebral
and just deeply effective approach.

00:11:16.339 --> 00:11:18.082
CA: But to reach the top level,

00:11:18.106 --> 00:11:21.985
you have to have
sort of an ability to schmooze

00:11:22.009 --> 00:11:23.829
a bit more than was natural for you?

00:11:23.853 --> 00:11:25.854
Because you had
this painful moment, right?

00:11:25.878 --> 00:11:28.109
When you were pulled aside
and [someone] said,

00:11:28.133 --> 00:11:30.823
"You know, that partner thing
you maybe were hoping for?